@article{ref240,
    abbrev_source_title = "Educ. Chang.",
    abstract = "This article argues that poetry is an act of meditation, improvisation   and exploration, and urgency is what guides the writer into (and   through) the poetic journey. In the light of this, this article   illustrates the features of a workshop that was designed to guide social   and human scientists in the delicate process of turning raw data into   poems. One of the chief objectives of the decolonial project is to   bridge the gap between Westernised academia (''The Ivory Tower'')   and communities where research is conducted, and this article aims to   show how poetic inquiry is a fitting research methodology that can serve   this purpose. Through a description of the workshop process and specific   poems that emerged from it, it suggests that poetic inquiry is an   innovative and effective research methodology for social and human   scientists engaged in the transformation of conventional knowledge   production.",
