@article{ref245,
    abbrev_source_title = "Eur. J. Commun.",
    abstract = "This article explores datawalking as a novel method in media and   communication research for studying datafication. Drawing from existing   literature, datawalking is characterized as an embodied, situated and   generative practice. These affordances of walking help to tackle   existing research challenges and connect lived experiences to data   infrastructural concerns. More specifically, contemporary research on   the deep mediatized city faces challenges that pertain to the   invisibility, loss of context and access to data and its   infrastructures. It is argued that datawalks, as an empirical method in   media and communication research, offers a much-needed anchoring of data   as material and situated, and constitutive of everyday life.",
