@article{ref250,
    abbrev_source_title = "Vis. Commun. Q.",
    abstract = "This study quantifies the effectiveness of information recall with   direct and indirect labeling of the annotation layer in a news data   visualization. Variations of three data visualizations from The New York   Times, The Washington Post, and The Wall Street Journal were presented   to participants in a crowdsourced experiment to measure their story   comprehension. Our results demonstrate that direct labeling offers no   advantage over indirect labeling. More significantly, annotations on   visualizations do no better to enhance comprehension than visualizations   without them, contradicting data visualization orthodoxy.",
